An :ENDWHILE that closes an :IF when no :WHILE is open anywhere: the
truly-crossed case of mismatched_block_end, ranged on the :ENDWHILE. The
:IF stays on the stack and is reported as unclosed_block at end of file
(diag.mismatched_block_end, diag.unclosed_block).
-- input.ssl --
:DECLARE bReady, nCount;
bReady := .T.;
nCount := 0;
:IF bReady;
	nCount := 1;
:ENDWHILE;
-- format --
:DECLARE bReady, nCount;

bReady := .T.;
nCount := 0;

:IF bReady;
	nCount := 1;
:ENDWHILE;
-- diagnostics --
4:1-4:4 error unclosed_block: Unclosed ':IF' - expected ':ENDIF'
6:1-6:10 error mismatched_block_end: ':ENDWHILE' does not match ':IF'
-- diagnostics [--strict --info] --
4:1-4:4 error unclosed_block: Unclosed ':IF' - expected ':ENDIF'
6:1-6:10 error mismatched_block_end: ':ENDWHILE' does not match ':IF'
